	(text "Current Sense Circuit sim for internal MCU Opamp.\n\nFor this esc, the internal opamps in the motor driver will be leveraged in an effort to save on signal integrity, as it is differential \npairs compared to the signle eded opamps offered directly on the stm32. \nInternal Opamp can only amplify with gains of 5, 10, 20, and 40. Thus, this had to be taken into consideration when sizing the shunt resistor, \nalong with resolution adn power constrainrs. A 3m resistor was selected in order to maximize the total ADC usage (85%) while keeping power constaints in mind.\n\nUsing a 3m resistor, and a gain of 16, for the rated 20A, the min and max ADC values are 0.374 and 2.931 respectively.\nThis ensured around a 10% margin on the ADC\n\nWith a max of 22A, the peak power dissipated will be 1.452W, or the time average value of 0.726W.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 421.386 113.538 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b953ff88-5596-4aaf-a171-e407524be4f2")
	)
